`_ddg_taint_reaches` gains an optional `escape_sites` out-param recording every
`(symbol_id, line)` at which the walk lost track. Purely observational: the
verdict is identical whether or not it is passed.

WHY THIS IS PRODUCTION CODE AND NOT AN INSTRUMENT. INV-busis's shape split
decides whether ~79% of its blockers are genuine escapes or misclassified
expression reads, and that split needs to know which line each walk died at. The
instrument that produced the filed split re-derived the walk's escape logic
OUTSIDE the walk, lives in a dead session scratchpad, and no longer matches this
signature — which the item records as its own durability hazard. A measurement
that re-implements the thing it measures drifts from it (L2).

WHAT IT FOUND, on hypergumbo self-analysis: 150 escape sites, 66 resolved to a
CFG statement. The largest bucket — 24 of 66 (36.4%) — has a node type of
literally `call`, and 99 of 150 (66%) have NO callee recorded at that line.
Positive control: `subprocess.run` IS recorded at other sites, so the empties
are real absences rather than a dead argument.

The sites name the cause themselves:

    print(
    isinstance(stderr, bytes)
    cmd.append("-q")

Those are calls. INV-mumov already measured why they carry no edge — Python
emits ZERO call edges for attribute-chain receivers and none for a builtin bare
`Name`. No edge means no `callees_at` entry, which means `_use_site_terminates`
cannot decide whether the callee consumes the value, which means `escaped =
True` and the walk returns None.

SO INV-mumov IS MANUFACTURING INV-busis'S BLOCKERS. A substantial share of the
"genuine non-call escape sites" that make the §7a/§7b scope ruling look
load-bearing are calls made invisible by a separate, already-filed,
false-negative defect that needs no owner ruling at all. On this sample the
expression-read family is 42.4%, not 78.6%, and the largest single bucket is not
an escape category. Neither item's thread mentioned the other; both now do.

CAVEATS, load-bearing and recorded on the items: Python ONLY — the three Go
repos on this machine yielded 15 resolved sites between them, far too few to
quote as shares, and caddy/pretix (where the filed 81 came from) are not here.
Self-analysis, not a neutral corpus. The `assignment` bucket does not separate
plain assignment from field write, so its 19.7% is an upper bound. Raw node
types are published beside every bucket so the histogram stands without the
shape naming, which is the one editorial part.

INSTRUMENT ERROR, recorded because it nearly became a headline: a first pass
read positional `a[5]` for `callees_at` and got a clean 100% have-no-callee.
`a[5]` is `summaries`; `callees_at` is `a[4]`. The flat 100% is what gave it
away (L11: distrust clean extremes).

The two branches this adds that no CORE test reached — the seeding escape (a
source line the DDG recorded nothing for) and the followed-but-unaccounted call
(WI-votom hole 2's shape) — now have tests. The full suite passed at 21999 while
core sat at 99% in isolation: a mainstream test was covering core's lines, which
`check-package-coverage` caught and CI would only have caught after a push.

